# Failure handling

## RPT ID not found

```json
{
  "status": "NOT_FOUND",
  "message": "No RPT was found for RPT-10025."
}
```

The reasoning model must not create a summary.

## Multiple primary records found

```json
{
  "status": "DATA_INTEGRITY_ERROR",
  "message": "Multiple primary records were found for RPT-10025."
}
```

Do not automatically select one.

## Client name missing

```text
Client ID: CLIENT-101
Client name: Unavailable
```

Do not invent the name.

## MongoDB timeout

```json
{
  "status": "DATABASE_TIMEOUT",
  "retryable": true
}
```

Retry through application-controlled retry logic, not through uncontrolled LLM loops.

## Missing required field

```json
{
  "status": "PARTIAL_DATA",
  "missing_fields": [
    "totalRebate"
  ]
}
```

The final answer should state:

```text
Total rebate information is unavailable.
```

# Final responsibility map

| Component          | Responsibility                                         |
| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| Input Guardrail    | Validate and protect the request                       |
| Intent Router      | Identify what the user wants                           |
| Entity Extractor   | Extract explicit IDs and values                        |
| Context Resolver   | Resolve “it,” “that client,” dates and session context |
| SOP Retriever      | Retrieve approved business procedures                  |
| Metadata Retriever | Retrieve real collections, fields and relationships    |
| Planner            | Decide what must be fetched and processed              |
| MQL Generator      | Convert the plan into MongoDB syntax                   |
| MQL Validator      | Validate schema, security and performance              |
| MongoDB Executor   | Execute the controlled query                           |
| Result Validator   | Check data completeness and consistency                |
| Summary Agent      | Apply business reasoning and generate the summary      |
| Response Validator | Check grounding and SOP compliance                     |
| Audit Service      | Store traceability and operational metrics             |

# Most important design

```text
User query
    ↓
Understand request
    ↓
Resolve context
    ↓
Retrieve SOP
    ↓
Retrieve metadata
    ↓
Create plan
    ↓
Generate validated MQL
    ↓
Execute MongoDB query
    ↓
Validate returned data
    ↓
Apply business reasoning
    ↓
Validate and return the answer
```

The essential principle is:

```text
Metadata tells the system what data exists.

Business SOP tells the system what the business expects.

Planner decides what work must be performed.

MQL Generator decides how MongoDB should retrieve the data.

Reasoning Agent explains the validated data.
```

